From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Harris <chris.harris@discordapp.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 09:58:55 -0700
Subject: gpu_info_util: close X11 display on success path

The success path in GetNvidiaDriverVersionWithXNVCtrl returned without
calling XCloseDisplay, leaking the X11 connection opened at the top of
the function. On NVIDIA systems where the query succeeds this happens
on every call, which over time can exhaust X server client slots and
file descriptors.

Move (or rather add) the cleanup to the early-return path so the
connection is closed regardless of outcome.

diff --git a/src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_x11.cpp b/src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_x11.cpp
index dcd4d17e7103e8c25f44ae64d01dc6f4750aa514..304a58ba721a1dc080e65ade39c8d7264cea05b6 100644
--- a/src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_x11.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_x11.cpp
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ bool GetNvidiaDriverVersionWithXNVCtrl(std::string *version)
                 ASSERT(buffer != nullptr);
                 *version = buffer;
                 XFree(buffer);
+                XCloseDisplay(display);
                 return true;
             }
         }
